    <!--
        ============================================================================
        Concrete themes (Phase 2A)

        A theme only declares:
          * the semantic design-system tokens (dsColor* / dsShape*), and
          * the legacy custom attributes whose meaning is screen specific.

        Everything else (Material3 colour roles, dialog/sheet/popup/input
        theming, legacy token mapping, shapes, typography) is inherited from
        AppTheme.NoActionBar in values/styles.xml.

        Legacy themes (DefaultLight*, DefaultDark*, Amoled*) keep their stored
        preference ints (Common/ThemeEnums.cs) and their palettes. The token
        layer only fills the shared window/launch background with the same
        Material light/dark background the legacy themes used before; no legacy
        palette value was dropped. New installs default to ModernLight /
        ModernDark (see Seeker/Helpers/PreferencesManager.cs).
        ============================================================================
    -->

